# mtplx-131k-stable-bench
owner: looker · cadence: every 2h · status: SUGGESTED
**Want a nightly 131K benchmark that collapses the contested figures into one stable number?**

## Prompt
Run the Qwen 27B MTPLX Optimized Speed setup at exactly 131K context on the 32GB Mac with --memory-budget 32GB and a fixed large prompt. Record decode tok/s, prefill tok/s, and peak memory. If the run completes and the new figure differs from wiki/comparisons/mtplx-131k-speed-report-comparison.md by more than 15 percent, archive the old contested figures into a dated conflict note (keep contested: true) and write the new figure as the stable result.

## Evidence
> 14-19 tok/s decode, 46 tok/s prefill at 131K
> 8.2 tok/s at 131K while testing with a large 131K prompt
> There is a 131K result on record, but the reported figures are not consistent
